# UP6b, correction C1: the withdrawable flag survives every rewrite of the row. Bob's absence Remove
# is voided at its TTL and re-driven twice in its epoch, then carried across the epoch by the
# re-issue a resync's external commit triggers; bob's resume still withdraws it.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group call kind=call target=eaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaea community=none creator=alice
join bob call via=external
sync alice
join carol call via=external
sync alice
sync bob
absent bob call
advance_clock 35s
advance_clock 35s
resync carol call
sync alice
resume bob call withdrawn=1
sync alice
commit alice call
sync bob
send alice call bob is still in
expect_decrypts bob call bob is still in
